1
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:48,320
That was just a dream... right?

2
00:01:01,210 --> 00:01:06,250
In the face of absolute despair

3
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:10,250
That nearly burned
our hearts away

4
00:01:11,750 --> 00:01:16,800
You still found the
courage to smile

5
00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:21,600
Like you accepted it all

6
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:24,860
I lost my voice

7
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:27,480
And the things I wanted to say

8
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:32,730
But every time I
fell to my knees

9
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:37,030
I stood up and kept walking

10
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:42,700
We were looking for
the ideal white future

11
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:47,930
Our one and only hope

12
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:50,420
Now I may be left with nothing

13
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:55,840
But these raging
emotions that have

14
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:58,940
Nowhere to go

15
00:01:59,190 --> 00:02:04,190
Still, I'll look for a new dawn

16
00:02:04,570 --> 00:02:07,600
With more than one right answer

17
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:11,430
I won't stop

18
00:02:11,730 --> 00:02:13,460
Until I find it

19
00:02:20,170 --> 00:02:24,500
Winter Days, Where the Heart Is

20
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:51,029
Were you holding back today?

21
00:02:51,030 --> 00:02:52,030
No.

22
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:56,989
It felt like you weren't being as
hard on me as you were yesterday.

23
00:02:56,990 --> 00:02:59,790
That is because your
abilities have improved.

24
00:03:00,870 --> 00:03:01,870
They have?

25
00:03:02,210 --> 00:03:05,670
To be precise, your form no
longer has any wasted movement.

26
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:07,799
Really?

27
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:10,260
I was only mimicking
his moves, though.

28
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:16,100
So you are basing your technique
on Archer's style and not mine.

29
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:19,599
You can tell that?

30
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,019
Of course.

31
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:24,899
After all, you had no form
of your own to begin with.

32
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:28,110
I'm sorry. I didn't mean it as
a slight against you, Saber.

33
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:33,660
I guess he was in my head because
I was around him all day yesterday.

34
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:36,740
There's no need to apologize.

35
00:03:37,490 --> 00:03:41,909
If Archer's style is
a better fit for you,

36
00:03:41,910 --> 00:03:43,579
it isn't my place to judge.

37
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:44,750
Um, Saber...

38
00:04:15,570 --> 00:04:16,570
Good morning.

39
00:04:17,910 --> 00:04:20,449
Hey. It's not often
we see you late.

40
00:04:20,450 --> 00:04:23,120
Fujimura-sensei
was pretty irate.

41
00:04:24,210 --> 00:04:27,210
Finally gracing us
with your presence?

42
00:04:30,170 --> 00:04:31,299
Shinji...

43
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:34,800
I guess you're feeling pretty
badass after what happened.

44
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:37,550
Still, I'm glad you came.

45
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:42,310
If you weren't here,
it wouldn't be any fun.

46
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,409
What's up? Not
going to the cafeteria?

47
00:05:06,410 --> 00:05:08,669
I'd like to, but...

48
00:05:08,670 --> 00:05:10,630
Well, see for yourself.

49
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:17,509
There can be no doubt.

50
00:05:17,510 --> 00:05:21,350
That lady peeks into our classroom—
Nonchalant, yet brazen as can be.

51
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:26,769
It is clear she waits not for one who does
not come but for one who does not notice.

52
00:05:26,770 --> 00:05:30,019
She looks about to snap, like one who
left a birthday gift for another to find,

53
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:35,860
only for it to remain undiscovered
by the recipient for the entire year.

54
00:05:55,170 --> 00:05:57,469
Where are you going, Tohsaka?

55
00:05:57,470 --> 00:06:01,179
It's lunchtime, so I'm
obviously going to eat lunch.

56
00:06:01,180 --> 00:06:02,639
Oh, right.

57
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:04,969
Well, find a nice spot.

58
00:06:04,970 --> 00:06:07,229
I'll be eating in the
student council office.

59
00:06:07,230 --> 00:06:09,349
Wait just one minute!

60
00:06:09,350 --> 00:06:12,769
What, did you forget your
lunch money or something?

61
00:06:12,770 --> 00:06:14,689
I can share my
lunch with you if...

62
00:06:14,690 --> 00:06:17,280
Of course I didn't,
you blithering idiot!

63
00:06:26,950 --> 00:06:29,080
You'll be sitting in
the wind over there.

64
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:54,980
Sorry.

65
00:06:57,070 --> 00:06:58,820
About yesterday, I mean.

66
00:06:59,690 --> 00:07:01,910
I've used a Command
Spell on Archer.

67
00:07:02,660 --> 00:07:06,660
I ordered him not to attack you for any
reason as long as our alliance stands.

68
00:07:08,450 --> 00:07:12,460
I know it doesn't make up
for anything, but I'm sorry.

69
00:07:13,710 --> 00:07:17,210
That isn't something you
should be apologizing for.

70
00:07:18,210 --> 00:07:23,050
It was my fault for letting him
run off by himself yesterday.

71
00:07:23,930 --> 00:07:25,259
Okay.

72
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:27,850
If that's what you
say, I'll go along with it.

73
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:31,139
Besides, I was partly to blame,

74
00:07:31,140 --> 00:07:33,100
and if he hadn't
been there, I...

75
00:07:35,110 --> 00:07:37,190
Let's call it even.

76
00:07:38,610 --> 00:07:39,610
Yeah.

77
00:07:41,070 --> 00:07:43,909
So where's Archer today?

78
00:07:43,910 --> 00:07:45,739
I left him at home.

79
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:46,740
Oh.

80
00:07:48,740 --> 00:07:51,660
Crap, lunch
break's already over!

81
00:07:54,750 --> 00:07:56,500
Hang out with me for a bit.

82
00:07:57,500 --> 00:08:00,130
Skipping class every once in a
while won't do any harm, right?

83
00:08:11,730 --> 00:08:14,600
Why are you so fixated
on fortification magic?

84
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:19,610
I've tried several kinds, but
that's the only one I can do.

85
00:08:20,190 --> 00:08:24,949
I can store simple spells,
alter the flow of mana,

86
00:08:24,950 --> 00:08:28,779
and channel it into
various holding places.

87
00:08:28,780 --> 00:08:30,200
Should you be telling me this?

88
00:08:30,700 --> 00:08:33,870
You told me your specialty,
so it wouldn't be fair if I didn't.

89
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:41,459
I showed you earlier,
but this is my magic crest.

90
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:44,550
In the Tohsaka family, we pass
down channeling techniques.

91
00:08:45,010 --> 00:08:50,100
Our specialty is the transfer of power,
either within ourselves or to others.

92
00:08:54,930 --> 00:08:58,810
Did you know that the
Matous are a mage family?

93
00:08:59,310 --> 00:09:00,399
Yes.

94
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:04,570
But Father told me that they're no
longer considered a bloodline of mages.

95
00:09:06,110 --> 00:09:07,359
Wait a second!

96
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:09,530
You knew that
Shinji was a Master?

97
00:09:12,990 --> 00:09:16,040
Sorry! I just found
out this morning.

98
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:20,040
I'd written him off as someone
who couldn't possibly be a Master.

99
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:22,959
What are you going
to do about him?

100
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:25,169
Attack him right away?

101
00:09:25,170 --> 00:09:29,469
I wouldn't just attack someone out
of nowhere solely for being a Master.

102
00:09:29,470 --> 00:09:31,719
Wow. You could've fooled me.

103
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:35,429
I only attacked you because
you weren't taking this seriously.

104
00:09:35,430 --> 00:09:37,190
It was an exceptional exception!

105
00:09:38,310 --> 00:09:42,649
Anyway, our enemy is the other
Master that's been hiding at this school.

106
00:09:42,650 --> 00:09:44,780
Let's focus on them for now.

107
00:09:46,690 --> 00:09:50,779
So you're saying there are
four Masters here at school?

108
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:52,200
Wouldn't there have to be?

109
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:56,119
Shinji has no power
as a Master himself.

110
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:59,869
I told him I'd turn a blind
eye if he behaved himself,

111
00:09:59,870 --> 00:10:01,789
so I don't expect
any trouble from him.

112
00:10:01,790 --> 00:10:03,499
Wait, Tohsaka...

113
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:06,210
Tell me more about that.

114
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:09,589
Shinji was the one who
approached me, originally.

115
00:10:09,590 --> 00:10:13,929
He said, "Since we're both
Masters, shall we join forces?"

116
00:10:13,930 --> 00:10:17,230
Naturally, I turned him down, but
he wouldn't take no for an answer.

117
00:10:17,770 --> 00:10:18,890
So finally, I said,

118
00:10:19,270 --> 00:10:23,859
"I already have Emiya-kun,
so I don't need you."

119
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:26,070
Right to his face!

120
00:10:27,490 --> 00:10:30,240
So that's why he was
acting so strangely.

121
00:10:31,110 --> 00:10:33,370
Well, what's the plan, Tohsaka?

122
00:10:34,990 --> 00:10:40,210
Shinji might not be a mage, but
he was the one who put up that field.

123
00:10:43,750 --> 00:10:45,960
You didn't realize?

124
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:48,129
Oh, no!

125
00:10:48,130 --> 00:10:49,470
Shinji might...

126
00:11:11,110 --> 00:11:12,569
That's great!

127
00:11:12,570 --> 00:11:15,530
This is how
Servants ought to be!

128
00:11:41,310 --> 00:11:43,019
What's going on?

129
00:11:43,020 --> 00:11:46,560
Keep generating mana
within your body, Emiya-kun.

130
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:48,650
Sakura!

131
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:08,840
Wai...

132
00:12:26,150 --> 00:12:27,479
She's breathing.

133
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:29,569
It isn't too late to save them.

134
00:12:29,570 --> 00:12:32,440
We have to find Shinji
and take down this field.

135
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:43,620
Emiya-kun!

136
00:13:03,470 --> 00:13:05,019
What are these things?

137
00:13:05,020 --> 00:13:06,099
Golems.

138
00:13:06,100 --> 00:13:07,650
A type of familiar!

139
00:13:11,190 --> 00:13:12,610
I'll summon Saber.

140
00:13:14,190 --> 00:13:16,740
You used a Command
Spell yesterday, right?

141
00:13:17,660 --> 00:13:20,070
That means it's my turn.

142
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,410
Emiya-kun...

143
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:33,500
I beseech you.

144
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:34,800
To my side,

145
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:36,720
Saber!

146
00:13:59,780 --> 00:14:00,740
Saber!

147
00:14:00,741 --> 00:14:03,239
I have come in response
to your summons.

148
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:04,620
Master, the situation?

149
00:14:04,990 --> 00:14:06,369
It's as you can see.

150
00:14:06,370 --> 00:14:08,539
A Servant has set
up a magic field.

151
00:14:08,540 --> 00:14:10,499
I want to dismantle it
as quickly as possible.

152
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:11,960
Archer, do you hear me?

153
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:16,419
I sense the presence
of a Servant on this floor.

154
00:14:16,420 --> 00:14:18,009
No way! Here?

155
00:14:18,010 --> 00:14:19,010
Rin?

156
00:14:19,510 --> 00:14:22,800
Well, if that's what you sense,
then I'm sure you're right.

157
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:26,059
But I sense the field's point of
origin as being on the first floor.

158
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:30,809
It's coming from the first floor
even though the Servant is here?

159
00:14:30,810 --> 00:14:34,729
I can't say for sure,
but that's what I sense.

160
00:14:34,730 --> 00:14:37,489
Rin, where is Archer?

161
00:14:37,490 --> 00:14:40,489
We could make a better
assessment with him here.

162
00:14:40,490 --> 00:14:43,369
I'm calling him, but
he isn't answering!

163
00:14:43,370 --> 00:14:46,739
This field cuts us off
from the outside world.

164
00:14:46,740 --> 00:14:48,910
A Command Spell is
our only means of contact.

165
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:54,210
We should consider this a field
designed to separate Master from Servant.

166
00:14:55,130 --> 00:14:58,050
The enemy is planning to
settle things here, Shirou.

167
00:15:00,630 --> 00:15:04,220
Saber, there's a Servant
on this floor, right?

168
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:07,639
You handle that one.

169
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:09,559
We're going to bring
down that magic field.

170
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:11,099
Emiya-kun?

171
00:15:11,100 --> 00:15:13,900
A risky move, but
the correct one.

172
00:15:15,730 --> 00:15:17,479
Now, while I keep them busy.

173
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:19,069
Thanks.

174
00:15:19,070 --> 00:15:20,320
Let's go, Tohsaka.

175
00:15:21,030 --> 00:15:22,450
Damn it!

176
00:15:31,210 --> 00:15:33,039
CHEMISTRY ROOM

177
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:34,999
Very good.

178
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,170
This is how a first-rate
Master does things.

179
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:43,010
Once this is over, maybe I'll go
check out Emiya's withered husk.

180
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:52,190
What is it, Rider?

181
00:15:55,810 --> 00:15:58,269
Hey, what's the deal?

182
00:15:58,270 --> 00:15:59,280
How are you able to move?

183
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:04,740
Stay away, damn it.

184
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:07,910
I'm warning you,
you'd better stay away!

185
00:16:08,950 --> 00:16:10,120
What the hell?

186
00:16:13,660 --> 00:16:15,080
Rider!

187
00:16:44,570 --> 00:16:46,240
Rider-class Servant...

188
00:17:14,020 --> 00:17:15,020
Caster...

189
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:20,649
Tohsaka, did you locate
the field's point of origin?

190
00:17:20,650 --> 00:17:22,149
Yes, it's right over there.

191
00:17:22,150 --> 00:17:24,070
- That room up ahead!
- CHEMISTRY ROOM

192
00:17:24,073 --> 00:17:25,700
Damn, they're persistent!

193
00:17:28,110 --> 00:17:30,450
Is there no end to these guys?

194
00:17:30,780 --> 00:17:32,290
Shirou, stand back.

195
00:17:34,870 --> 00:17:36,330
- Ein Körper...
- A corpse...

196
00:17:36,333 --> 00:17:37,710
- Ist ein...
- is a...

197
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,000
- Körper!
- Corpse!

198
00:17:55,310 --> 00:17:57,020
Shinji!

199
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:05,399
Don't give me any
of your excuses.

200
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:09,359
I'll make you pay for what
you've done, no matter what!

201
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:12,159
Y-You've got it wrong!
You've got it all wrong!

202
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:14,700
It wasn't me! I
swear it wasn't me!

203
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:16,999
It wasn't you?

204
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,619
I don't care! Take this
field down right now!

205
00:18:19,620 --> 00:18:22,290
If you say no, I'll blow
your sniveling face clean off!

206
00:18:22,670 --> 00:18:26,589
I'm telling you, you've got it wrong!
It wasn't me! She was killed by...

207
00:18:26,590 --> 00:18:27,670
Shinji!

208
00:18:32,850 --> 00:18:35,099
Ouch, ouch...

209
00:18:35,100 --> 00:18:36,100
Tohsaka!

210
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:40,850
Tohsaka, over there.

211
00:18:55,580 --> 00:18:56,870
She's dead.

212
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:16,060
Looks like you abandoned
your Servant to survive.

213
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:19,979
But if you saw the killer's
face, it'll be your turn next.

214
00:19:19,980 --> 00:19:22,519
Th-That's not fair!

215
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:25,229
I don't have a Servant!

216
00:19:25,230 --> 00:19:26,230
I'm not a Master anymore!

217
00:19:26,770 --> 00:19:28,690
You two are the
ones they'll be after!

218
00:19:29,490 --> 00:19:30,859
That's true.

219
00:19:30,860 --> 00:19:34,909
Even if you still have Command
Spells, you're no threat.

220
00:19:34,910 --> 00:19:36,949
A gnat like you
can't kill anyone.

221
00:19:36,950 --> 00:19:38,699
A g-gnat?

222
00:19:38,700 --> 00:19:40,079
You're calling me a gnat?

223
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:43,250
Be glad I'm not comparing
you to a harmful bug!

224
00:19:44,330 --> 00:19:47,089
If you saw who
did it, tell me now.

225
00:19:47,090 --> 00:19:50,880
Right now, that's
all you're good for.

226
00:19:52,470 --> 00:19:53,380
Talk!

227
00:19:53,381 --> 00:19:56,509
Which Servant killed yours?

228
00:19:56,510 --> 00:19:58,680
Get bent, dumb-ass!

229
00:19:59,060 --> 00:20:02,690
Y-You're the ones
who should be scared.

230
00:20:03,060 --> 00:20:07,360
After all, you're the
ones it'll come after next!

231
00:20:17,030 --> 00:20:18,909
It's okay, Tohsaka.

232
00:20:18,910 --> 00:20:20,410
They're all still breathing.

233
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:22,200
They're breathing?

234
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:25,040
Yeah, they're alive.

235
00:20:25,370 --> 00:20:27,210
All we have to
do is call for help.

236
00:20:28,670 --> 00:20:31,880
Do they need an ambulance for
something like this? Or should we call...

237
00:20:32,420 --> 00:20:35,219
We should call the church.

238
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:38,220
If we explain the situation to
Kirei, he'll see to everything.

239
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:40,099
Okay.

240
00:20:40,100 --> 00:20:41,720
I'll call him right away, then.

241
00:20:47,690 --> 00:20:49,769
You were fighting Caster?

242
00:20:49,770 --> 00:20:54,650
Yes, although it was merely Caster's
shadow that controlled the familiars.

243
00:20:54,950 --> 00:20:59,739
I see. Then the real Caster
hasn't left Ryuudou Temple.

244
00:20:59,740 --> 00:21:04,040
Knowing her, she might have manipulated
Shinji to lure Rider into a trap.

245
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:08,170
Then Rider was killed
through deception?

246
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:09,669
Crap.

247
00:21:09,670 --> 00:21:14,549
Still, we know that Caster's
Master is someone at this school.

248
00:21:14,550 --> 00:21:15,550
Right...

249
00:21:16,970 --> 00:21:19,640
Tohsaka, if you have
something to say, then say it.

250
00:21:20,550 --> 00:21:23,429
You were really
level-headed, Emiya-kun.

251
00:21:23,430 --> 00:21:24,890
It took me by surprise.

252
00:21:25,430 --> 00:21:27,349
There was nothing
level-headed about it.

253
00:21:27,350 --> 00:21:29,400
If anything, I was
beside myself with rage.

254
00:21:29,690 --> 00:21:33,280
Even so, you were able to
assess everyone's injuries.

255
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:36,860
I could never manage that.

256
00:21:37,660 --> 00:21:39,700
It was no big deal.

257
00:21:40,450 --> 00:21:41,990
I'm used to seeing dead bodies.

258
00:21:44,830 --> 00:21:46,040
Used to it?

259
00:22:10,370 --> 00:22:16,509
We didn't understand anything

260
00:22:16,510 --> 00:22:22,679
My left hand groped for
things that vanished to my touch

261
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:25,679
A moral conflict

262
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:28,480
stays your hand

263
00:22:28,730 --> 00:22:31,229
and tricks you

264
00:22:31,230 --> 00:22:33,110
out of your future

265
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:40,029
I don't know how
to protect anyone,

266
00:22:40,030 --> 00:22:45,830
and my ideals might
well be pointless,

267
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:54,040
but I want to live my life

268
00:22:55,040 --> 00:23:00,049
The past repeats before my eyes

269
00:23:00,050 --> 00:23:07,849
Here I will trust the me
that now stands with you

270
00:23:07,850 --> 00:23:13,939
Until my dream
crumbles and withers,

271
00:23:13,940 --> 00:23:19,569
I hope you will carve
out paradise with me

272
00:23:19,570 --> 00:23:23,280
Fight your fate

273
00:23:27,010 --> 00:23:30,229
I'll find out whether
or not he's a Master.

274
00:23:30,230 --> 00:23:33,899
Anyone who isn't worthy of this
battle should be eliminated early on.

275
00:23:33,900 --> 00:23:35,769
You call yourself a hero?

276
00:23:35,770 --> 00:23:38,480
Then are you saying that you
still have the resolve to fight?

277
00:23:38,481 --> 00:23:40,990
The Distance Between Them

278
00:23:37,520 --> 00:23:40,990
Next Time

